---
description: Research Coach project rules
alwaysApply: true
---
# Product
Research Coach: a web app that guides undergrads through starting an
AI/ML research paper. Core differentiator: the AI never loses project
context. Structured project state in Postgres is the source of truth;
prompts are assembled from it on every call. Do NOT rely on chat history
for memory.

# Stack
Next.js App Router, TypeScript (strict), Supabase (auth, Postgres, RLS),
Anthropic API called from server routes only. Tailwind + shadcn/ui.

# Hard rules
- API keys only in server code. Never expose them to the client.
- Citations: the model may ONLY cite papers present in the `papers` table
  (fetched from Semantic Scholar/OpenAlex/arXiv). Never invent references.
- The AI coaches and critiques; it does not ghostwrite the paper.
- Model state changes are PROPOSED as patches; the user accepts/rejects.
- Prompt assembly is a pure function in `lib/prompt/assemble.ts` with unit tests.
- All tables use Row Level Security scoped to auth.uid().
- Validate all API inputs with zod. Validate model tool output before saving.
- Small, reviewable commits. Explain what you changed after each task.

# Scope
MVP = Phase 1 (Orient) and Phase 2 (Find your question) only.
Do not build experiment or paper-writing features yet.